<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Habsburg-Lorraine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1736">1736</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Habsburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a> was the dynasty founded by the marriage in 1736 of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa">Maria Theresa</a>, heiress of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> lands, and Francis Stephen, duke of Lorraine, later Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i-holy-roman-emperor">Francis I</a>. Its members ruled the Habsburg Monarchy, then the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a>, until 1918, and held the Grand Duchy of Tuscany until 1859 and other Italian states.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-habsburg-lorraine.jpg" alt="House of Habsburg-Lorraine" width="320" height="309" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SEPB66 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wapen_van_Habsburg-Lotharingen.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The last duke, Francis Stephen, married Maria Theresa and became Holy Roman Emperor; their house of <b>Habsburg-Lorraine</b> ruled Austria until 1918.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-lorraine">Duchy of Lorraine · At a glance</a></li></ul></section>
